<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan tenders to buy Jun 11-20 unleaded reformate.</title>
<headline>Taiwan tenders to buy Jun 11-20 unleaded reformate.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) has issued a tender to buy unleaded 95-octane reformate for delivery in June 11-30, a company official said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The tender, which closes May 5 and is valid for two days, seeks a 250,000-barrel cargo on a cost-and-freight (c-and-f) basis for delivery to Keelung, Taichung, Kaohsiung or Shalung.</p>
<p>In its last tender, CPC bought an unexpectedly large three unleaded and one leaded cargo for May 16-31 and June 1-15 arrival and $24.60-24.70 per barrel and $25.20, respectively, on a c-and-f basis.  </p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-8703093)</p>
</text>
